  "dom_id": "step-q141522",
  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "Complete the square on the quadratic expression ${x}^{2}+x-2.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}x-2\n$$\n\nNow, here's the trick. We *add* and *then subtract* ${(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2},$ writing the constant term $-2$ last:\n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}x+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}}_{\u23df}-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-2\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-2\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n{(x+\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{9}{4}.\n$$",
